}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-04-04 11:24] observe — the current hook performs staged file collection, check execution, report rendering, and Touch ID authorization in one shell surface.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:24] observe — poll-review and the hook overlap semantically but do not yet read like two surfaces of one shared review engine.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] decide — redesign around informed authorization: checks first, summary second, authorization last.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] decide — plan a shared review runner plus narrower renderer and authorization boundary so the hook becomes orchestration instead of policy ballast.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] taste — the highest-value improvement is making the human authorize a concrete commit summary, not just a generic biometric prompt.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[json_surface]: "Should the shared review runner emit JSON as a first-class artifact now, or only after the shell refactor lands?"
 ?[inspect_mode]: "Should inspect-before-authorize open `git diff --cached --stat`, full diff, or a focused risk summary first?"
 ?[agent_source]: "Is explicit `SPW_AGENT` enough for agent attribution, or should the wrapper persist a small context file for stronger provenance?"
}

